      "claim": "A regeneration holds the lane's lock for as long as it runs, so seats' hand-ins wait behind it. Resolve holds the lane's exclusive installation lock (a blocking flock) for the whole run, including the regeneration, which has no time limit by ruling R-35-m3. Every seat's hand-in (work land calls plain.HandIn), Say, landing return, prove and push wait on that lock until the command ends or landing stop kills it. Step 1 works and is safe without a change: nothing is lost or written wrongly, landing status still reads, and landing stop (which does not need this lock) ends a stall.",
      "evidence": "metasystem/internal/landing/plain/resolve.go:71 holds withLock across the runRegeneration call at line 241. metasystem/internal/landing/plain/queue.go:87-97 and metasystem/internal/lock/file.go:24-34 show the lock blocks (LOCK_EX without LOCK_NB). HandIn takes the same lock at queue.go:229.",
